# Response headers on Cloudflare Pages, copied to build/_headers. docs/hosting.md § Headers says why
# each is here and what another host needs instead. Paths are from the domain root: a build with
# BASE_PATH needs them prefixed. A request matching several rules gets every rule's headers, and two
# values for one header are joined with a comma, so Cache-Control is set by one rule per path only.
# Pinned by src/headers.test.ts.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

# Named by their hash, so a new build gives a new name.
/_app/immutable/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Pages and data keep their names between builds. Private: they sit behind the sign-in, and the
# data may be real, so no shared cache keeps a copy.
/
  Cache-Control: private, no-cache

/*/
  Cache-Control: private, no-cache

/*.html
  Cache-Control: private, no-cache

/data/*
  Cache-Control: private, no-cache
